{"id": "unknown-2026-07-24-003", "date": "2026-07-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India concludes WTO review on tariffs, FTAs and trade reforms", "content": "India’s eighth Trade Policy Review has concluded at the WTO in Geneva, with 68 WTO Members intervening across two July sessions.\nFor textile and apparel exporters and importers, the review signals continued scrutiny of tariffs, customs, quality orders and trade remedies.\nIndia said reforms, FTA strategy and customs simplification support a predictable trade and investment regime.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-concludes-wto-review-on-tariffs-ftas-and-trade-reforms-312042-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-24-004", "date": "2026-07-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["optimistic", "growth", "improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "India's Trident Group Q1 profit rises 55% QoQ to $1.58 mn", "content": "Indian home textiles company Trident Group reported a strong Q1FY27 performance, with consolidated income rising 9.3 per cent QoQ to ₹1,803 crore (~$18.03 million) and net profit increasing 55 per cent to ₹158 crore (~$1.58 million). \nImproved yarn prices, cost discipline, and operational efficiencies supported margin expansion. \nThe company remains optimistic about export growth. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-trident-group-q1-profit-rises-55-qoq-to-1-58-mn-312040-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-24-005", "date": "2026-07-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Can India unlock $7 bn in apparel exports without new capacity?", "content": "India could add several billion dollars in garment exports by improving planning, utilisation and delivery, but the full $7 billion upside is not idle capacity.\nTexPro data shows India’s selected-market apparel share barely moved from 2021 to 2025 as Bangladesh, Vietnam and Cambodia gained.\nExporters must first reverse 2026 declines, then build capability in sweaters, outerwear and MMF-rich", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/can-india-unlock-7-bn-in-apparel-exports-without-new-capacity--312037-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-24-006", "date": "2026-07-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "ICE cotton gains modestly, weak export demand limits rally", "content": "ICE cotton futures extended gains for a fourth straight session, supported by stronger crude oil prices and broader strength in agricultural commodities.\nHowever, weak US export sales, a firmer US dollar and light trading capped gains.\nTraders continue to monitor weather, export demand, Brazil's larger crop outlook and China's reserve auctions.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-gains-modestly-weak-export-demand-limits-rally-312038-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
